Joan, Professor Cushman and the others.

2253
01:14:41,471 --> 01:14:42,951
- [Tom] I need some Carmex, now.

2254
01:14:42,951 --> 01:14:44,725
- I need some money.

2255
01:14:44,725 --> 01:14:46,431
A lot of money.

2256
01:14:46,431 --> 01:14:47,885
- [Mike] Please see the bursar.

2257
01:14:47,885 --> 01:14:49,605
- I'll do anything I can to help you,

2258
01:14:49,605 --> 01:14:52,031
but we don't keep very
much money in the house.

2259
01:14:52,031 --> 01:14:55,461
- Cliff's doing alright for himself.

2260
01:14:55,461 --> 01:14:57,781
You've probably got a lot of jewels.

2261
01:14:57,781 --> 01:14:59,208
(car horn beeping)

2262
01:14:59,208 --> 01:15:00,288
- Good evening, Mr. Scott.

2263
01:15:00,288 --> 01:15:02,195
- Hello, I'm sorry you
have to stay out here.

2264
01:15:02,195 --> 01:15:03,529
- Oh, that's alright, sir, it's my job.

2265
01:15:03,529 --> 01:15:04,362
Good night.

2266
01:15:04,362 --> 01:15:05,195
- Good night.

2267
01:15:05,195 --> 01:15:06,881
- [Crow] By the way, you
mind if a smoke out here?

2268
01:15:06,881 --> 01:15:07,714
Right.

2269
01:15:08,565 --> 01:15:10,085
