my Whitey Ford rookie card.

2320
01:16:27,639 --> 01:16:28,491
- I'll take it.

2321
01:16:28,491 --> 01:16:29,324
- But it's locked.

2322
01:16:29,324 --> 01:16:31,038
I keep the key in the desk drawer.

2323
01:16:31,038 --> 01:16:32,371
- I won't need a key.

2324
01:16:32,371 --> 01:16:34,118
- But, Hal, there's personal papers in it.

2325
01:16:34,118 --> 01:16:36,558
Things of no value to you,
but very valuable to me.

2326
01:16:36,558 --> 01:16:38,185
I'd like to keep them if you don't mine.

2327
01:16:38,185 --> 01:16:39,718
- Okay, unlock it.

2328
01:16:39,718 --> 01:16:41,958
Remember, I'm watching you.

2329
01:16:41,958 --> 01:16:43,785
- [Crow] Ah, the flexible burglar.

2330
01:16:43,785 --> 01:16:46,478
- [Tom] So, Hal, you going
to the reunion next month?

2331
01:16:46,478 --> 01:16:48,225
I hear the gang's getting back together.

2332
01:16:48,225 --> 01:16:50,078
Joan Bemis is bringing a banjo.

2333
01:16:50,078 --> 01:16:51,245
Should be fun.

2334
01:16:52,546 --> 01:16:53,945
- [Mike] That's chemistry answers.

2335
01:16:53,945 --> 01:16:55,705
You won't need that.

2336
01:16:55,705 --> 01:16:57,745
