2352
01:17:24,638 --> 01:17:26,438
(door rattling)
(rushing orchestra music)

2353
01:17:26,438 --> 01:17:27,838
- [Tom] Oh, poor fellow, probably needs

2354
01:17:27,838 --> 01:17:28,911
to use the bathroom.

2355
01:17:28,911 --> 01:17:29,965
(door rattling)

2356
01:17:29,965 --> 01:17:31,151
(door opens)

2357
01:17:31,151 --> 01:17:32,538
- What's going on, I heard a shot.

2358
01:17:32,538 --> 01:17:33,497
- It's Hal Moffat.

2359
01:17:33,497 --> 01:17:35,208
He's upstairs, my husband shot him.

2360
01:17:35,208 --> 01:17:37,248
- [Mike] Was he on his
tuffet at the time, ma'am?

2361
01:17:37,248 --> 01:17:39,081
- [Tom] Stop that now.

2362
01:17:40,811 --> 01:17:42,331
- [Crow] This is really gonna cut into

2363
01:17:42,331 --> 01:17:43,664
my smoking time.

2364
01:17:44,765 --> 01:17:47,631
(scary orchestral music)

2365
01:17:47,631 --> 01:17:49,848
- Cliff!
- [Crow] Well, I, hmm?

2366
01:17:49,848 --> 01:17:51,428
(ominous orchestral music)

2367
01:17:51,428 --> 01:17:55,518
- [Tom] Maybe, no, I can't
take his last cigarette.

2368
01:17:55,518 --> 01:17:57,068
- No.

2369
01:17:57,068 --> 01:18:01,845
- [Mike] Well, good luck,
however, it turns out.

2370
01:18:01,845 --> 01:18:04,511
- Calling cars 41 and 53, district 5.

2371
01:18:04,511 --> 01:18:05,538
- [Crow] Guess who?

2372
01:18:05,538 --> 01:18:07,791
- Cars 41 and 53, district 5.

2373
01:18:07,791 --> 01:18:11,511
Proceed at once to 500
block, Cottage Grove Avenue.

2374
01:18:11,511 --> 01:18:13,605
Investigate a 341.

2375
01:18:13,605 --> 01:18:14,645
- [Tom] Write this down.

2376
01:18:14,645 --> 01:18:15,578
- Proceed with caution.

2377
01:18:15,578 --> 01:18:17,231
This job is by the creeper.

2378
01:18:17,231 --> 01:18:19,698
- [Tom] Hubcaps are alerted

2379
01:18:19,698 --> 01:18:22,338
(sirens blaring)

2380
01:18:22,338 --> 01:18:24,431
- [Mike] It was right around the corner.

2381
01:18:24,431 --> 01:18:26,485
- [Crow] So, this is a Persian rug.

2382
01:18:26,485 --> 01:18:28,563
- There's another one.

2383
01:18:28,563 --> 01:18:29,625
Oh, yes.

2384
01:18:29,625 --> 01:18:30,611
- [Mike] Oh, mama.

2385
01:18:30,611 --> 01:18:31,505
- He's been hit alright.

2386
01:18:31,505 --> 01:18:32,338
- [Tom] Oh, baby.

2387
01:18:32,338 --> 01:18:33,862
Now maybe he's been hurt badly enough

2388
01:18:33,862 --> 01:18:34,703
to slow him up.

2389
01:18:34,703 --> 01:18:36,418
- [Officer] Captain Donelly?
- Yeah.

2390
01:18:36,418 --> 01:18:37,985
- We just got a flash on the radio.

2391
01:18:37,985 --> 01:18:38,923
They've traced him to the Tanna district,

2392
01:18:38,923 --> 01:18:39,829
over by Grand Avenue.

2393
01:18:39,829 --> 01:18:40,696
- Maybe.

2394
01:18:40,696 --> 01:18:41,923
- Hey, you know what I think?

2395
01:18:41,923 --> 01:18:42,756
- Yeah, I know.

2396
01:18:42,756 --> 01:18:44,976
- [Tom] You're a large, pink smelly man.

2397
01:18:44,976 --> 01:18:47,616
(ominous orchestral music)

2398
01:18:47,616 --> 01:18:49,656
- [Mike] Oh, boy, this could mean an early

2399
01:18:49,656 --> 01:18:52,869
and unexpected end to his creeping career.

2400
01:18:52,869 --> 01:18:56,794
- [Crow] Yeah, the creeper
is on the 15 day DL.

2401
01:18:56,794 --> 01:18:59,563
(ominous orchestral music)

2402
01:18:59,563 --> 01:19:00,980
- [Mike] Matthew!

2403
01:19:02,059 --> 01:19:03,392
- [Tom] Justice.

2404
01:19:04,646 --> 01:19:07,899
- [Crow] Oh, god, how the hell did she

2405
01:19:07,899 --> 01:19:10,766
ever get a piano up here?

2406
01:19:10,766 --> 01:19:13,006
Okay, once I get you
her, I have to ask her

2407
01:19:13,006 --> 01:19:15,256
to move to the first floor.

2408
01:19:16,459 --> 01:19:21,046
- [Tom] Oh, they're going
to visit Mr. Kotter.

2409
01:19:21,046 --> 01:19:23,219
(metal clanking)

2410
01:19:23,219 --> 01:19:24,993
- [Tom] Um, hello, anybody there?

2411
01:19:24,993 --> 01:19:27,493
- [Mike] Hello?
- [Tom] Hello?

2412
01:19:28,766 --> 01:19:30,046
- [Mike] You know, one thing I have to say

2413
01:19:30,046 --> 01:19:31,606
for this creeper, he
really opened the door

2414
01:19:31,606 --> 01:19:33,189
for other creepers.

2415
01:19:34,073 --> 01:19:36,023
- [Crow] Ladies and Gentlemen,

2416
01:19:36,023 --> 01:19:39,276
in the center ring, the
creeper will now attempt

2417
01:19:39,276 --> 01:19:41,023
the high thing.

2418
01:19:41,023 --> 01:19:43,809
(laughing)

2419
01:19:43,809 --> 01:19:45,369
- [Tom] I should have
called her and told her

2420
01:19:45,369 --> 01:19:47,896
to meet me at the drug store.

2421
01:19:47,896 --> 01:19:49,869
- [Mike] Man, such a
nightmare for all creepers

2422
01:19:49,869 --> 01:19:52,576
to blow out a knee or get shot like this.

2423
01:19:52,576 --> 01:19:55,043
- [Crow] So he's in pain and it's taking

2424
01:19:55,043 --> 01:19:56,003
him a long time.

2425
01:19:56,003 --> 01:19:57,763
- [Tom] So mostly like before, then.

2426
01:19:57,763 --> 01:20:01,180
(upbeat synth pop music)

2427
01:20:03,596 --> 01:20:06,703
(moves to ominous orchestral music)

2428
01:20:06,703 --> 01:20:11,023
- [Tom] Geez, I wish
I'd worn my gym clothes.

2429
01:20:11,023 --> 01:20:13,276
- [Mike] Oh, god, my trick groin.

2430
01:20:13,276 --> 01:20:14,584
- [Crow] Boy, he's had several injuries

2431
01:20:14,584 --> 01:20:19,169
that don't really help his
chances with women, at all.

2432
01:20:19,169 --> 01:20:23,009
- [Mike] It feels good just to not creep.

2433
01:20:23,009 --> 01:20:26,926
- [Tom] Ah, ha, and that's
significant because?

2434
01:20:28,756 --> 01:20:31,797
- [Mike] Ah, bet I look like hell.

2435
01:20:31,797 --> 01:20:34,903
(strained orchestral music)

2436
01:20:34,903 --> 01:20:37,416
- [Crow] Honey, my face is as big as ever

2437
01:20:37,416 --> 01:20:40,083
and someone shot my sizzler off.

2438
01:20:41,075 --> 01:20:45,189
(strained orchestral music)

2439
01:20:45,189 --> 01:20:46,022
- Helen.

2440
01:20:46,022 --> 01:20:46,855
- [Tom] Ah!

2441
01:20:46,855 --> 01:20:47,688
Don't do that.

2442
01:20:47,688 --> 01:20:49,623
- Hal, you startled me.

2443
01:20:49,623 --> 01:20:51,543
You came in by the fire escape.

2444
01:20:51,543 --> 01:20:52,983
Are you in trouble again?

2445
01:20:52,983 --> 01:20:55,493
- No, I've got something for you.

2446
01:20:55,493 --> 01:20:57,639
- [Crow] A transformer I
got with my happy meal.

2447
01:20:57,639 --> 01:20:59,239
- [Mike] (gasps) Steelies.
- [Helen] What's this?

2448
01:20:59,239 --> 01:21:01,359
- This stuff will enough
for that operation.

2449
01:21:01,359 --> 01:21:04,106
- [Tom] You mean my cath implants?

2450
01:21:04,106 --> 01:21:06,883
- Where did you get these?

2451
01:21:06,883 --> 01:21:08,016
Hal, you're hurt.

2452
01:21:08,016 --> 01:21:09,869
- [Crow] I hear blood.

2453
01:21:09,869 --> 01:21:11,523
- I'm alright.

2454
01:21:11,523 --> 01:21:13,349
You have that operation right away.

2455
01:21:13,349 --> 01:21:14,536
- [Crow] Can't it wait until morning?

2456
01:21:14,536 --> 01:21:15,536
- Hal, wait!

2457
01:21:18,400 --> 01:21:19,800
(ominous orchestral music)

2458
01:21:19,800 --> 01:21:21,453
I'd like an appraisal of these jewels.

2459
01:21:21,453 --> 01:21:23,133
- [Tom] They came from a
wounded guy with a hole

2460
01:21:23,133 --> 01:21:25,480
in his groin and won't
let me touch his face.

2461
01:21:25,480 --> 01:21:27,573
- [Crow] Eh, this is a daredevil lure.

2462
01:21:27,573 --> 01:21:28,586
- Yes, ma'am.

2463
01:21:28,586 --> 01:21:29,920
It'll take a few minutes.

2464
01:21:29,920 --> 01:21:31,000
Would you care to wait?

2465
01:21:31,000 --> 01:21:32,573
- Yes, I'll wait.

2466
01:21:32,573 --> 01:21:34,920
- [Mike] Okay, go ahead and wait, then.

2467
01:21:34,920 --> 01:21:37,587
Start waiting, right over there.

2468
01:21:39,510 --> 01:21:40,926
- [Tom] This stuff is hotter than

2469
01:21:40,926 --> 01:21:42,926
a Pasadena tennis court.

2470
01:21:45,089 --> 01:21:47,089
- [Crow] Wow, he got his
name legally changed.

2471
01:21:47,089 --> 01:21:48,195
- [Tom] What do you know.

2472
01:21:48,195 --> 01:21:49,329
- [Mike] Astoundingly little detail in

2473
01:21:49,329 --> 01:21:50,996
this robbery detail.

2474
01:21:52,609 --> 01:21:54,635
- [Tom] And one rock
that might be an agate.

2475
01:21:54,635 --> 01:21:57,210
- [Crow] That's an odd recipe.

2476
01:21:57,210 --> 01:22:00,009
(ominous orchestral music)

2477
01:22:00,009 --> 01:22:03,259
- [Mike] Mrs. Robinson, I got the room.

2478
01:22:05,181 --> 01:22:08,259
- Operator, get me the police.

2479
01:22:08,259 --> 01:22:11,100
- What did he say when
he gave you these jewels?

2480
01:22:11,100 --> 01:22:12,699
- He told me to sell
them and use the money

2481
01:22:12,699 --> 01:22:15,339
for an operation on my eyes.

2482
01:22:15,339 --> 01:22:18,059
- Didn't you think that
was a little funny?

2483
01:22:18,059 --> 01:22:19,685
- I started to ask him about them,

2484
01:22:19,685 --> 01:22:22,005
but he left before I had the chance.

2485
01:22:22,005 --> 01:22:23,632
- Don't you realize you can get yourself

2486
01:22:23,632 --> 01:22:25,979
into a lot of trouble
protecting a criminal?

2487
01:22:25,979 --> 01:22:27,339
- [Tom] Let me put it this way, have you

2488
01:22:27,339 --> 01:22:29,662
every seen Chained Heat?
- [Helen] A criminal?

2489
01:22:29,662 --> 01:22:32,599
- Well, I think you can call him that.

2490
01:22:32,599 --> 01:22:34,225
- [Mike] Hmm, back me up on this, Roy?

2491
01:22:34,225 --> 01:22:35,559
- I can't believe it.

2492
01:22:35,559 --> 01:22:37,292
- Didn't you know the
police were after him.

2493
01:22:37,292 --> 01:22:38,166
- No.

2494
01:22:38,166 --> 01:22:39,280
- Not even that first night, when they

2495
01:22:39,280 --> 01:22:41,227
came to your room?

2496
01:22:41,227 --> 01:22:42,626
- I thought they were just some men.

2497
01:22:42,626 --> 01:22:43,667
- [Crow] With badges and guns.

2498
01:22:43,667 --> 01:22:45,027
- He never told me.

2499
01:22:45,027 --> 01:22:47,527
- No, no, I guess he wouldn't.

2500
01:22:48,577 --> 01:22:50,377
- I knew he was in some sort of trouble

2501
01:22:50,377 --> 01:22:52,577
but I didn't realize
it was with the police.

2502
01:22:52,577 --> 01:22:53,937
- [Crow] I thought he was pregnant.

2503
